<title>USA: Hemagen gets okay on autoimmune test kit.</title>
<headline>Hemagen gets okay on autoimmune test kit.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hemagen Diagnostics Inc said Wednesday that it has obtained clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market a new test kit for the detection of autoimmune related diseases.</p>
<p>The company said its Virgo Anti-Cardiolipin screening ELISA test kit is used to aid in the screening of patient serum for the presence of autoantibodies that are typically observed in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus and other connective tissue diseases.</p>
